# Vitest --detect-async-leaks ceiling for the web dashboard suite.
# See docs/design/web-http-adapter.md for the investigation + the
# matrix of approaches that don't help.
#
# Raise this only after verifying the source of additional leaks is
# mechanical (a new test surface, a new hook fixture) rather than a
# regression. Lower it whenever the MSW matching layer or the store
# teardown landscape improves.
#
# Local count is ~75; CI runs land in the 90-91 band after the
# storage-shim landed (down from ~96 before). The ceiling carries a
# 3-leak buffer above the observed CI peak so the gate doesn't false-
# fail on natural run-to-run variance, while still tightening the
# ratchet against regressions.
#
# The CI step reads this file via:
#   grep -v '^#' .github/ci/web-async-leaks.max | head -1
94
